  <info><link type="guide" xref="canvas"/><desc>Revisions and Attachments in coyote.</desc></info>
  <title>Revisions and Attachments</title>
  <p>Select one saved revision in <gui>Drawings and revisions</gui> to display that exact revision. Selection and <gui>Show in Canvas</gui> are display-only: neither replaces nor discards a working draft. There is no separate <gui>Edit Revision</gui> command. When a displayed revision is writable and <gui>Show Markup</gui> is on, Pencil, Eraser, and Crop are available. A completed stroke or <gui>Apply Crop</gui> starts a working copy based on the displayed revision. Canvas saves any unsaved changes in the previous working copy as a new revision before switching; browsing, zooming, and canceled gestures or crops do not change drafts. Save creates an immutable child revision only when the working copy differs from its base; saving unchanged content creates no duplicate. Original revisions, prior saved revisions, and attachments already staged in the composer are never overwritten by editing or saving.</p>
  <p>Use <gui>Selected</gui> → <gui>Attach</gui> to freeze selected revisions or the working copy. Reorder or remove attachments in the composer. <gui>Send</gui> uploads the exact native-size PNGs in that order; it does not crop or resize them. In replay, <gui>Show in Canvas</gui> displays the exact recorded revision when its editable data is available, without replacing or switching any working draft.</p>
</page>
